  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "Amelia and Blake take turns rolling a die. Amelia rolls first. The first player to roll a 1 loses. Find the probability that Amelia wins.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{5}{11}$.\n\nAmelia wins if Blake rolls a 1 first; if neither rolls a 1, the situation resets.",
      "worked": "Let $p$ be the probability that Amelia eventually wins. She wins in the first pair of rolls if she avoids a 1 and Blake rolls a 1. If both avoid a 1, the situation resets with winning probability $p$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}p&=\\frac{5}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}\\times\\frac{5}{6}\\times p\\\\p&=\\frac{5}{36}+\\frac{25p}{36}\\\\36p&=5+25p\\\\11p&=5\\\\p&=\\frac{5}{11}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 57
  },
